-- title:
--   Unique polynomial representatives for evaluation with a monic kernel generator
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a field, $A$ a commutative ring, $\phi:K\to A$ a unital ring homomorphism, and $x\in A$. Let $m\in K[T]$ be monic. Write $E(q)=q_\phi(x)$ for polynomial evaluation, and assume the exact kernel criterion
--   $$
--   E(q)=0\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad m\mid q
--   $$
--   for every polynomial $q\in K[T]$.
--
--   For each $q$, let $R_q$ be its remainder on division by $m$. Then $\deg R_q<\deg m$ and $E(R_q)=E(q)$. Moreover, every polynomial $r$ satisfying $\deg r<\deg m$ and $E(r)=E(q)$ equals $R_q$.
--
--   For every pair of polynomials $q,r$,
--   $$
--   E(q)=E(r)\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad R_q=R_r.
--   $$
--   The target ring may be trivial, and the monic generator may have degree zero. We use $\deg0=-\infty$; when $\deg m=0$, the unique representative is zero. The exact kernel hypothesis is part of the statement and ensures uniqueness.
-- source:
--   Derived supporting algebra lemma for the Senthil Kumar mission. Uses polynomial division by a monic polynomial in Mathlib at revision 0df444a360eaa60ab8c11dca51a86af692955474: degree_modByMonic_lt, modByMonic_eq_self_iff, eval₂_modByMonic_eq_self_of_root and modByMonic_eq_of_dvd_sub in Algebra/Polynomial/Div.lean, lines 147-154, 210-213, 609-611 and 662-666. Sources: https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/blob/0df444a360eaa60ab8c11dca51a86af692955474/Mathlib/Algebra/Polynomial/Div.lean#L609-L611 and https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/blob/0df444a360eaa60ab8c11dca51a86af692955474/Mathlib/Algebra/Polynomial/Div.lean#L662-L666. Assumes the evaluation kernel is exactly the ideal generated by the specified monic polynomial. Its remainder is the unique representative of smaller degree, and two evaluations agree exactly when their remainders agree. This result is derived here, not quoted from the article. No new definitions or platform theorem dependencies. Trivial target rings and monic polynomials of degree zero are allowed.

import Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Div

theorem WeierstrassEllipticZeta.polynomial_monic_evaluation_normal_form
    (K A : Type*) [Field K] [CommRing A]
    (φ : K →+* A) (x : A) (m : Polynomial K) (hm : m.Monic)
    (hker : ∀ q : Polynomial K, q.eval₂ φ x = 0 ↔ m ∣ q) :
    (∀ q : Polynomial K,
      (q %ₘ m).degree < m.degree ∧ (q %ₘ m).eval₂ φ x = q.eval₂ φ x ∧
        ∀ r : Polynomial K, r.degree < m.degree → r.eval₂ φ x = q.eval₂ φ x →
          r = q %ₘ m) ∧
      ∀ q r : Polynomial K, q.eval₂ φ x = r.eval₂ φ x ↔ q %ₘ m = r %ₘ m := by sorry
